<title>FRANCE: French sugar consumption down in March - FIRS.</title>
<headline>French sugar consumption down in March - FIRS.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>French sugar consumption declined to a provisional 150,000 tonnes in March from 152,000 tonnes in February and from 155,900 tonnes in March 1996, national sugar intervention board FIRS said on Monday.</p>
<p>This would bring cumulative sales to the French market for the first six months of the 1996/97 season (Oct/Sept) to 954,200 tonnes against 916,201 tonnes in the same period for 1995/96, data from the FIRS report for May showed.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
</text>
